e.gov.uk/media/69de23bb3e81003ae042250c/s300_DfE_Sanctuary_Building_London_office.jpeg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department <br/>for Education"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Education","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-education","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","base_path":"/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","content_id":"845e63b4-c0f1-11e4-8223-005056011aef","details":{"body":"<p>The Secretary of State is responsible for the work of the Department for Education, including:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>early years and childcare</li>\n  <li>children’s social care</li>\n  <li>teacher quality, recruitment and retention</li>\n  <li>the school curriculum</li>\n  <li>school improvement</li>\n  <li>academies and free schools</li>\n  <li>further education</li>\n  <li>apprenticeships and skills</li>\n  <li>higher education</li>\n</ul>\n\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":16,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2022-11-08T09:31:05Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Secretary of State for Education","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/education/safeguarding-pupils","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/education/safeguarding-pupils","base_path":"/education/safeguarding-pupils","content_id":"b67afac3-0bfc-4e44-9893-951be4d05e4c","description":"Keeping children safe in education, including guidance around drugs, radicalisation and gangs.","details":{"internal_name":"Safeguarding pupils","notes_for_editor